==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹæptə/|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-raptor.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹæptɚ/|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|æptə(ɹ)|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|rap|tor}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|id=bird of prey|:inh|enm:raptour}}
From {{inh|en|enm|raptour}}, from {{der|en|la|raptor|t=kidnapper, thief}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|en|rapter||obsolete}}
* {{alt|en|raptour||obsolete|rare}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[bird of prey]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} One who [[ravish]]es or [[plunder]]s.

=====Derived terms=====
{{col|en|raptorish|raptorlike}}

=====Related terms=====
{{col3|en|oviraptor|raptorial}}

=====Translations=====
{{trans-see|bird of prey}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ety|en|id=dinosaur|:clipping|velociraptor}}
Popularized (and possibly coined) in 1990 by {{w|Michael Crichton}} in ''[[w:Jurassic Park (novel)|Jurassic Park]]''; {{clipping|en|velociraptor|nocap=1}}, ultimately of the same etymology as above.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|informal|paleontology}} One of the [[dromaeosaur]]s, a family of [[carnivorous]] [[dinosaur]]s having [[tear]]ing [[claw]]s on the [[hind leg]]s.

