==English==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:der|fr:réalité|tree=1}}
From {{der|en|fr|réalité||quality of being real}}, from {{der|en|frm|realité||property, possession}}, from {{der|en|la-med|reālitās}}, from {{der|en|la-lat|reālis||real}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|real|ity}}. Recorded since 1550 as a legal term in the sense of “fixed property” (compare {{m|en|real estate}}, {{doublet|en|realty|notext=1}}); the sense “real existence” is attested from 1647. {{etydate|c|1540}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹiːˈælɪti/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹiˈæləti/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-reality.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ælɪti|s=4}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# The state of being [[actual]] or [[real]]; [[realness]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''reality''' of the crash scene on TV dawned upon him only when he saw the victim was no actor but his friend.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|title=The Exploring Series|episode=Exploring the SCP Foundation: Pattern Screamers|date=7 January 2019|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=404z0snK_Qs|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230111141843/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=404z0snK_Qs|archivedate=11 January 2023|accessdate=11 January 2023|time=0:11|text=While the SCP universe is, of course, filled with things that we would certainly not consider "real", most of the SCPs are tangible or perceivable in some way.  There ''are'' those concepts, however, whose '''reality''' is debatable, even to the SCP Foundation, begging them to ask the question of what, exactly, is real.}}
# {{senseid|en|Q9510}} The [[real world#English:_Q9510|real world]].
#* {{RQ:Spectator|III|291|February 2 1712|passage=A man very often fancies that he understands a critic, when in '''reality''' he does not comprehend his meaning.}}
#* {{RQ:Birmingham Gossamer|chapter=I|passage=As a political system democracy seems to me extraordinarily foolish,{{nb...}}. My servant is, so far as I am concerned, welcome to as many votes as he can get.{{...}}I do not suppose that it matters much in '''reality''' whether laws are made by dukes or cornerboys, but I like, as far as possible, to associate with gentlemen in private life.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Emmanuel Tsekleves|title=Science fiction as fact: how desires drive discoveries|magazine=w:The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/media-network/2015/aug/13/science-fiction-reality-predicts-future-technology|date=2015-08-13|passage=Does this mean that '''reality''' has caught up with science fiction?|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160618073242/https://www.theguardian.com/media-network/2015/aug/13/science-fiction-reality-predicts-future-technology}}
# A [[real]] [[entity]], [[event]]{{,}} or other [[fact]].
#: {{ux|en|The ultimate '''reality''' of life is that it ends in death.}}
#: {{ux|en|There are several new '''realities''' that this team now needs to accept: our old project is dead, and our new project is now the priority.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=7|passage=And to '''realities''' yield all her shows.|year=1873}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1770|author={{w|James Beattie (poet)|James Beattie}}|title=Essay on the Nature and Immutability of Truth
|passage=My neck, Sir, may be an idea to you, but to me it is a '''reality'''.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1983|album=w:In A Special Way|author=w:Debarge|title=A Dream|text=A dream, of simple fantasy / That I, wished was '''reality''' / That you'd, come knocking at my door / And we'd, relive this dream once more}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1996|month=September|journal=Gay Community News|page=22|author=Doreen Drury|title=The Gay Capital of the World|text=Recent historical studies indicate that we must continue to challenge the notion that there is an unproblematic story of queer liberation. For example, how do local histories account for '''realities''' such as the increased racial segregation of the New York bar scene after Stonewall?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=European Court of Human Rights|title=Wypych v. Poland|date=2005-10-25|url=https://hudoc.echr.coe.int/eng?i=001-71236|issue=2428/05|passage=Given the economic '''realities''' of contemporary Poland, a requirement to provide information on movable assets which exceed PLN 10,000 in value cannot be held to be excessive.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Sam Leith|title=Sam Leith's top 10 alternative realities|magazine=w:The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/books/2011/may/11/sam-leith-top-10-alternative-realities|date=2011-05-11|passage=Exploring alternative '''realities''' isn't just a game for boys. In 1666, Margaret Cavendish, the Duchess of Newcastle, published a utopian fantasy of compelling strangeness.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210307154336/https://www.theguardian.com/books/2011/may/11/sam-leith-top-10-alternative-realities}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-07|author=w:Joseph Stiglitz| volume=188| issue=26| page=19| magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly| url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/commentisfree/2013/may/27/globalisation-is-about-taxes-too|title=Globalisation is about taxes too| passage=It is time the international community faced the '''reality''': we have an unmanageable, unfair, distortionary global tax regime. It is a tax system that is pivotal in creating the increasing inequality that marks most advanced countries today{{nb...}}.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210410210118/https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2013/may/27/globalisation-is-about-taxes-too}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Sonia Sodha|title=It’s time to ditch the stereotypes and look at the realities behind singledom|magazine=w:The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2018/sep/08/its-time-to-forget-stereotypes-realities-singledom|date=2018-09-08|passage=But part of me was still glad to see this undoubtedly superficial take. As a society, we barely discuss the '''realities''' and implications of singledom. In pop culture singledom is almost invariably represented as an easily fixed unhappy state, a step along the way to getting happily hitched.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20201109041413/https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2018/sep/08/its-time-to-forget-stereotypes-realities-singledom}}
# The [[entirety]] of all that is [[real]].
#* {{quote-av|en|author=w:Russell T Davies|director=w:Graeme Harper|actor=w:Julian Bleach|role=w:Davros|episode={{w|Journey's End (Doctor Who)|Journey's End}}|title=w:Doctor Who|date=5 July 2008|season={{w|Doctor Who (series 4)|4 [30]}}|number=13|text=Across the entire Universe.  Never stopping, never faltering, never fading.  People and planets and stars will become dust.  And the dust will become atoms and the atoms will become... nothing.  And the wavelength will continue, breaking through the rift at the heart of the Medusa Cascade into every dimension, every parallel, every single corner of creation.  This is my ultimate victory, Doctor!  The DESTRUCTION! Of '''REALITY'''!  ITSELF!}}
# An [[individual]] [[observer]]'s own [[subjective]] [[perception]] of that which is [[real]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} {{cap|loyalty}}; [[devotion]].
#* {{RQ:Fuller Holy State
|passage=To express our '''reality''' to the emperor.}}
# {{lb|en|legal|obsolete}} {{cap|realty}}; [[real estate]].
# {{lb|en|broadcasting|attributive}} {{U|reality television}}.
#: {{ux|en|a foray into '''reality''' programming}}

