{{en-verb|+|~ing,+}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To put oneself or itself at the end of a waiting line.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1959|month=April|author=B. Perren|title=The Essex Coast Branches of the Great Eastern Line|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=189|text=Although there is a spacious circulating area beyond the platforms at [[Clacton]], there is severe overcrowding on peak Saturdays; at times of pressure passengers have to '''queue''' out into the street [...]}}
