===Verb===
{{en-verb|+|+|+,~t<l:obsolete>}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cut]] (for example a grain) with a [[sickle]], [[scythe]], or reaping [[machine]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[gather]] (e.g. a harvest) by cutting.
#: {{syn|en|harvest}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Leviticus|19|9||And when ye '''reape''' the haruest of your land, thou shalt not wholly '''reape''' the corners of thy field, neither shalt thou gather the [[gleaning]]s of thy haruest.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To obtain or receive as a reward, in a good or a bad sense.
#: {{syn|en|harvest}}
#: {{ux|en|to '''reap''' a benefit from exertions}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Galatians|6|7||Be not deceiued, God is not mocked: for whatsoeuer a man soweth, that shall he also '''reape'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Regained|book=Samson Agonistes|page=60|passage=Why do I humble thus my ſelf, and ſuing / For peace, '''reap''' nothing but repulſe and hate?}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XLI|64|And what delights can equal those<br>⁠That stir the spirit’s inner deeps,<br>⁠When one that loves but knows not, '''reaps'''<br>A truth from one that loves and knows?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=11 June 2016|author=Phil McNulty| title=England 1-1 Russia| work=BBC Sport| url=http://www.bbc.com/sport/football/36450648| passage=England manager {{w|Roy Hodgson}} got plenty right with a positive selection and the decision to play {{w|Wayne Rooney|Rooney}} in midfield '''reaped''' a rich reward - but his boldest move may also have been his biggest mistake.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250830024200/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/36450648|archivedate=30 August 2025}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|computer science}} To terminate a child process that has previously exited, thereby removing it from the process table.
#: {{ux|en|Until a child process is '''reaped''', it may be listed in the process table as a zombie or defunct process.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To deprive of the beard; to shave.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 4-1|1|3|passage=Came there a certaine Lord, neat and trimly drest;<br>Fresh as a Bride-groome, and his Chin new '''reapt''',}}
# {{lb|en|euphemistic|slang}} To [[rape]].

